        Root cause:
        The root cause of the bug was the introduction of unnecessary memory barriers (`smp_mb()`) in the `_local()` variants of the atomic exchange functions in `xchg.h`. These barriers were added in previous commits, which led to incorrect memory ordering and potential performance issues. The original implementation had avoided these barriers, indicating that they were not needed for the correct functioning of the atomic operations.

        Commit message:
        locking/xchg/alpha: Remove superfluous memory barriers from
 the _local() variants

The following two commits:

  79d442461df74 ("locking/xchg/alpha: Clean up barrier usage by using smp_mb() in place of __ASM__MB")
  472e8c55cf662 ("locking/xchg/alpha: Fix xchg() and cmpxchg() memory ordering bugs")

... ended up adding unnecessary barriers to the _local() variants on Alpha,
which the previous code took care to avoid.

Fix them by adding the smp_mb() into the cmpxchg() macro rather than into the
____cmpxchg() variants.

